WEBVTT

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.940
How do you feel, Seeing?

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.590
The Day of Flicker

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.590
I'm fine... Although it feels 
strange sleeping next to Gauche.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:53.400
If that is all, good.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.390
A Heartometer...

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.290
With this, I can measure how much 
heart one has left, however...

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:03.140
Perhaps it's malfunctioning, but 
you've always registered at maximum.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.310
Doctor...

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.640
Where did Aria-san go on a delivery?

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.190
Oh, yes... She headed 
to a place called Astor.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.420
Astor? I've heard that name before...

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.820
Astor is the town in which the government 
examination airship crashed.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.450
Where the airship...

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.280
12 years ago...

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.300
The time when what came to be known 
as the Day of Flicker occurred.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.900
The day the artificial sun blinked off, and 
the entire world was engulfed in darkness.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.170
And the examination airship 
from the government crashed.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.640
Even today, the details of what happened 
to the artificial sun are unknown.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.450
I could never forget...

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.450
...what I saw that day.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.350
So this is Goodbye Amsterdam.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.900
It's quite a deep canyon. As dark as Yodaka.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.710
The cliffs block out the light 
from the artificial sun.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.010
You've got to have some serious 
issues to stay in Yuusari

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.050
but choose to live in a place like this.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.940
And he was one of the elite aboard 
the examination airship...

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.000
Franklin? Oh, the one 
with the scarred head...

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.180
If you're looking for him, he's in 
the house deepest in the valley.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.000
The deepest?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.900
He lives there all alone. 
I've hardly seen him.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.980
He's a bit...

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.240
No... He's completely mad. Be careful!

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.570
That's it!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.550
Mr. Franklin! Mr. Houdai Franklin!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.670
Delivery for you. Please open the door.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.690
I've come to deliver a letter.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.190
A letter, you say?

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.030
What... have... you come... for?

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.260
G-Go away!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.120
Aria!

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.620
Go away, fingers of the devil!

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.000
I won't be fooled again! Never again!

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.100
Are you perhaps mistaking 
us for someone else?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.300
You people once took me eye, 
my friend, my very life!

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:55.110
That... That... That dreadful thing!

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.560
Dreadful thing?

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.180
You mean the airship?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.700
Don't play dumb!

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.150
I saw it!

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:05.070
All you people in the government 
knew and said nothing, yes?

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.280
How could you say anything?

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.240
With that dreadful thing 
hanging in the sky...

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.300
...continuing to steal what 
people hold most dear!

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.300
Aria, should I make him hurt?

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:16.450
Should I get him?

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.120
Niche, just stay there.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.140
What did you see in the sky 
on that Day of Flicker?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.420
S-Stay back...!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.230
Mr. Franklin, please tell me...

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:28.660
Mr. Franklin...

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:33.250
I won't... let you steal anything more!

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:35.770
Aria!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.660
It wasn't just you.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:48.490
A person dear to me also looked upon that 
flickering light and lost a portion of his heart.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.950
The memories of his beloved mother.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.090
That person's life changed 
ever since that day.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:01.140
While he worked his heart out to make 
up for the gap left within it...

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.690
...he eventually lost his entire heart.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.600
According to the official 
government statement,

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.970
the airship crash was unrelated 
to the artificial sun.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.410
I don't believe that's the whole truth.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:21.320
But we haven't been told anything about 
what happened on the Day of Flicker.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:26.030
So if you know something, 
I want you to tell me.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.820
At least, believe me when I say this:

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.390
We are not your enemy.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:42.790
I've come to deliver something important 
to you, Mr. Houdai Franklin.  A letter.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.770
Who sent it?

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:50.040
A person named Negich.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.680
The family of my best friend, who 
died covering for me that day.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:01.370
I lost one eye and became mostly 
blind in the other through illness.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:04.260
I would much appreciate it 
if you would read it to me.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.780
In return, I will tell you 
what I saw on that airship.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:15.170
I apologize... I must tend to your injury.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:16.250
Come inside.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.910
Steak... Sylvette may be 100 
times stronger than Lag,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.490
but Aria might be even stronger than that.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:30.330
Like 500 times Lag.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:39.120
The airship "Progrès" was constructed 
to examine the artificial sun,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.290
and was built over hundreds of days 
in west Yuusari's Holden Caulfield.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:51.070
A great number of citizens of Yuusari, 
like myself, were put to work there.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:58.380
My friend Kamahan Negich and I were in 
charge of the elemental gas pressure.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.580
At the time, I was so overjoyed to 
have a job that seemed worth doing.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.600
But when I think on it now,

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.990
there was no way that a citizen of the capital 
would board a ship examining that dreadful thing...

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:17.000
It was all organized to use 
expendable people from Yuusari...

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:23.130
Only one person from the capital was on 
board, the general commander named Balor.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:24.530
Launch.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:25.210
Yes, sir!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:27.640
Pull!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.080
It's finally time, Houdai!

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:36.120
Yeah.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.300
Hey, Negich... Look at that.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.710
Kids are on board? Triplets?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.710
Those are Bees.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:46.590
Bees?

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:50.070
It'll be their hearts, 
amplified by Spirit Amber,

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.720
that will rotate the three propellers 
of the Progrès, after all.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.140
Thanks to that, we should reach 
our destination quite easily.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.140
Camus!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:00.100
Elena!

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.280
You came, Elena?

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.470
And Darwin, too!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.630
Of course, Camus. Congratulations.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.900
Wow... This thing's really going to fly?

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:11.970
Where's Lloyd?

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.280
He wasn't at home. Please forgive him.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.870
He may put a brave face on it, 
but he's having a tough time.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:24.800
Forgive him? If it wasn't for that chronic 
disease, it'd be Lloyd on the ship.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:27.370
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:31.720
But thanks to that, I can be 
together with Thane and Jean.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:36.380
Oh, I know! After the examination, you 
brothers will be able to enter the capital, right?

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.630
The three of you need to 
work hard for Largo's sake!

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.330
Yeah, thanks, Elena Bran.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.940
What is that fluffy tailed 
creature? I want to dissect it...

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.740
You were on the airship too, Doctor?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.360
Yes, I was replacing my father 
who had suddenly fallen ill.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:00.330
Apparently.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.400
Apparently?

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.400
That's what I was told as 
I lay on a hospital bed.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.400
I have no memories of that day.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:13.700
They were taken along with this eye.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:19.930
Not just me. Everyone on board that 
examination ship who saw the sun.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.560
I know that everyone had a piece of their 
heart and their body stripped away from them.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.060
T-That also happened to Gauche!

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.790
Gauche, as he looked at the flickering 
light from atop the hill,

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.900
lost the memories of his mother!

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:39.480
Are you saying that the light of 
the artificial sun stole his heart?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:42.620
Doctor, what in the world 
<i>is</i> the artificial sun?

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:44.930
Seeing!

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:48.850
This isn't good. Your fever is too high.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:50.610
Doctor...

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.790
Enough. We'll talk about this later.

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:57.510
The Heartometer is off the scale!

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:58.400
What?

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.000
Mo...ther...

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.710
What was the purpose of 
the examination exactly?

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.530
I wasn't important enough to know.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.350
However, during the construction of the 
Progrès, there was something I noticed.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:31.980
What's happening? Lately my 
eyes have been really tired.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.500
You too, Houdai?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.920
It's almost like I can't 
see as well as usual?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.420
What?

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.490
I hope it's just my imagination, 
but lately, the light...

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:48.180
I have a feeling like it's 
dimmer than it used to be.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.330
The light from the artificial 
sun was weakening?

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:52.490
It couldn't be...

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.700
I don't know it for a fact,

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.700
but it was definitely true at the 
time we were constructing the ship.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.940
And on that day, the 
airship Progrès took off.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.780
Open the fore valves! Memory 2500!

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:10.780
Evacuate the muddy waters!

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:14.150
Fore valves evacuating 2500!

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.910
It's been 12 years since then...

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:56.960
I thought it was weird that he didn't eat 
much breakfast this morning. But a fever, too?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.550
Lag goes so overboard just like my brother.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:04.180
Hurry! Give him greco and epiphone!

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.090
We've already given him 5 mgs!

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.580
Damn it, why won't it work?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.850
The Heartometer is still off the scale.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.840
We can't stop his heart from overflowing!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.650
At this rate he'll use it up completely!

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:17.460
Doctor?

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:21.310
Lag?

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.440
Mo...the...

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:55.060
These are all of Seeing's memories!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:14:00.390
Wait, there are images of things that 
I doubt could be in his memories...

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.570
And a number of frames not yet open.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.440
What in the world...

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.320
And what I saw in that sky...

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:11.850
It was...

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.830
How incredibly bright...

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.810
Dimming? I feel like it'll 
blind me from looking into it!

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:29.510
How did the capital create 
something like this?

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:34.350
If we go below the sun, maybe we 
could get a peak at the capital!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.100
Hey, Negich!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.810
What the... The light just went out?

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.320
Mother mother mother...

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.990
Mother mother mother...

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.750
Mother mother mother...

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.200
Mother mother mother...

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:53.990
Mother mother mother...

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.600
What is that?

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:05.950
Inside the sun, something 
like an eye opened up.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:10.260
I... I saw it! I saw it!

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:15.500
It peered into my heart... It stole my eye!

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.760
My eye! My eye!

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:24.900
Houdai, what's wrong? What happened?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.030
We're in a steep dive and the elemental 
pressure is extremely high!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.000
Hang in there!

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.250
What the hell are they 
doing on the ship's bridge?

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:35.330
Damn it!

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:43.160
What in the...

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.630
What happened, damn it!

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.890
Houdai, get into the gap in the frame!

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.340
The fever's receding?

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:18.600
I just had a dream...

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:23.120
A long, long dream...

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:32.790
Visions of this world, long long ago, 
so beautiful, so long forgotten...

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:35.200
Doctor...

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.740
Sylvette?

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:57.140
You have grown up...

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:03.730
Suede, is that you?

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.890
Gauche?

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:12.720
Lag... Lag Seeing, yes?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.450
I missed you.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:26.310
After that, I lost consciousness. 
When I woke up...

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.650
I heard that only 6 people survived.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.450
A young doctor...

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:44.390
Doctor Thunderland...

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:48.000
The man named Balor from the capital.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:52.280
The triplets who were on board the 
Progrès were gravely injured.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.290
It was a miracle even one of them survived.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.060
Jean, answer me! Answer me!

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:02.470
Thanks to Negich, my life was spared, but...

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:09.540
But next to me, he lay dead.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:18.280
That dreadful artificial sun stole 
the crew, my eye, and my best friend!

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.300
No matter how much I scream it 
out, no one even tries to listen!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.600
They call it the ravings of a madman!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.060
But they're wrong! It's 
not something to worship!

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.480
It's not something to pray to!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.350
That light is <i>alive</i>!

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.410
It consumes what is precious to people, 
so it can shine down on the world!

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.300
The price we pay for light is unfathomable!

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:45.770
It will continue on until one day 
it has consumed the entire world!

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.520
That's... impossible!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:51.480
I feel sorry for that person you hold dear.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:57.680
His heart became some of the light 
that was scattered upon the world.

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:02.470
G-Gauche...

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.140
Gauche!

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:07.700
It's already...

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:14.670
...beyond the point where it can 
be gathered and returned to him.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:46.690
Next: Welcome Home
